{
  "about": "The curated certificate seed of the Work token registry (workspace decision 0018, docs/product/engine.md, Token registry): certificates and licences as cert: tokens, source seed, never minted. A token is cert:<slug>, with :<region> where the credential is local (cert:electrician-license:us-tx, cert:nr-35:br). Levels and modules are metadata of the one token, not tokens of their own: levels are ordered lowest first and a level held serves every level below it; a module is an added part (a module, an endorsement, a specialty) and may imply others. names name the credential on their own; shared names (a state, an issuer of many credentials, NCCCO) name a family, so a string must also hold one of the credential's distinctive words, which the seed lists and no credential sharing a name or a state with it uses. excludes are words that make the string another credential, details words a worker's claim may carry that change nothing the plane reads, and requirements the phrases a hirer may use for it, in the regions where they mean it. fillers never change a credential, generic words never tell two apart, and notHeld phrases say a credential is not held. Public names of credentials only: no holder, no number, no personal data.",
  "version": "2026-10-24",
